 484: /**
 485:  * Tear down everything the test built â€” worlds first, then harnesses, last-opened-first within
 486:  * each â€” ATTEMPTING EVERY ONE and collecting the rejections rather than stopping at the first.
 487:  *
 488:  * Attempting all of them is the point: giving up after one rejection leaves the rest of the stack
 489:  * standing, and a frozen clock, an armed fault or a vendor counter that survives into the next id
 490:  * is exactly the cross-test leak the per-test teardown exists to prevent.
