 728:         //
 729:         // `h.sut[key]` is `unknown` and `h.fixtures.world()` is `WorldSeam`, because `h` is the
 730:         // concrete `AtHarness` the factory is checked to produce and that type deliberately says
 731:         // nothing about any one suite. No run-time value can prove its own static type, so this
 732:         // relabelling cannot be removed â€” only moved to where the claim is smallest.
 733:         //
 734:         // What changed is WHOSE claim it is. It used to be the suite's: `bindSuite<X, Y>` named two
 735:         // types and this line stamped them onto whatever the harness returned, so any pair of names
 736:         // was accepted. Now both come from `suite-adapters.ts`, which reads them off the adapter
 737:         // module that the `requirement` literal proves is the module `loadAdapter()` imports â€”
 738:         // checked at the map entry, and again at run time in `index.ts`.
 739:         //
