   4:  * Everything that used to live here â€” the AT id grammar, the tier contract (`AT_TIER`, no
   5:  * default), the harness handshake, per-test world/harness teardown, the `harness-missing` vs
   6:  * `sut-missing` split â€” now lives in the harness registry, so every suite gets the same
   7:  * contract from one implementation. This file supplies only what is REQ-016-specific: which
   8:  * member of `harness.sut` the suite drives, and how to say that it has not landed yet.
   9:  *
  10:  * ID BINDING is unchanged: every test is registered through `atTest(id, name, fn)`, the id is
  11:  * supplied ONCE at that call site, and the bijection checker reads those call sites.
  12:  */
  13: 
  14: import { bindSuite } from '../../harness/registry.ts';
